= Protocol (computing) — Technical =

A protocol specification can define syntax, semantics, timing, error handling, state machines, and extensibility rules. Layered architectures compose protocols so that higher layers can depend on services provided by lower layers without reproducing their internal mechanisms.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* protocol ≠ implementation
* protocol ≠ API
* protocol ≠ data format alone

== References ==
* IETF RFC 1122, ''Requirements for Internet Hosts — Communication Layers'' (1989).
* Andrew S. Tanenbaum and David J. Wetherall, ''Computer Networks'', protocol layering discussions.
* IETF RFC 2119 / RFC 8174, normative requirement terminology used in protocol specifications.
